NAME
    regs - dump CPU, video, APU, and coprocessor registers

SYNOPSIS
    regs
    regs <cpu>

DESCRIPTION
    Prints the attached core's main CPU, video (PPU), and (when reported)
    APU and coprocessor registers, formatting each value to its actual bit
    width. All reads use side-effect-free debug accessors so dumping
    registers never acknowledges interrupts or alters hardware state.

    Passing a processor name from cpus(1) prints only that processor's
    register set. The coprocessor section of bare 'regs' displays the
    processor named by the 'cop' alias (the first listed after the main
    CPU other than SPC700).

    'regs' is strictly read-only; use setreg(1) to modify a register.

EXAMPLES
    regs
    regs cpu
    regs spc
    regs gsu

EXIT STATUS
    0   Registers printed (or unknown-processor message printed).
    1   No target attached or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    setreg(1), cpus(1), eval(1), cophist(1), copflow(1), summary(1)
